This project is a basic console-based Bus Reservation System developed in the C programming language. It simulates the process of booking and managing bus seats, making it useful for understanding fundamental programming concepts such as structures, arrays, and user interaction.

The system allows users to:
View available seats
Book a seat by entering passenger details
Cancel an existing reservation

Each seat is managed using a structured data type that stores seat number, occupancy status, and passenger name.

🚀 Features
Simple and user-friendly menu-driven interface
Real-time seat availability display
Seat booking with passenger name
Reservation cancellation functionality
Input validation for seat numbers

🛠️ Technologies Used
C Programming Language
Standard Libraries (stdio.h, stdlib.h, string.h)

📚 Project Objective
The main goal of this project is to provide a basic understanding of how reservation systems work by automating seat booking and reducing manual errors.

